; CARRY-1 (2026-09-19) — THE FEEL COMPONENT. Every prop in this game is a RigidBody3D carrying
; BOTH NetworkedProp (its authority: who holds it, where the server says it is) and Interactable
; (its feel: how heavy it reads in the hand, where it rides, how it is posed). The split is the
; whole architecture — the authority layer never asks how a thing feels and the feel layer never
; decides who owns it — and it only works if both are actually on the prop.
;
; What it is read for here: HeftKg (this body's own Mass, times HeftScale) is the single number
; the carry spring turns into lag, droop, swing and squash, so a heavy prop lags in the hand AND
; thuds when it lands from the same value. HoldOffset/HoldRotationDegrees are where and how it
; rides. Nothing else on this component runs in-game: the hover hull is the lab's, and a
; networked grab goes through Carryable, never through Interactable.OnGrabbed.

[node name="Interactable" type="Node" parent="."]
script = ExtResource("2_interactable")
